# Copy to .env and fill in. With nothing set, everything defaults to the
# local docker stack (docker-compose.yaml): the integration suite generates
# every seed, key and deployment it needs and appends the values here as it
# goes, so a fresh clone runs green with an EMPTY environment.
#
# Naming convention: a MIDNIGHT_/EVM_ prefix says which chain a value lives
# on. Wallet seeds end _WALLET_SEED. Every address names what it points at:
# deployed code ends _CONTRACT_ADDRESS and an account ends _ACCOUNT_ADDRESS,
# so a bare _ADDRESS is a defect one grep finds. Key material names its half
# (_PRIVATE_KEY/_PUBLIC_KEY), which makes the secrets exactly the names
# ending _SEED or _PRIVATE_KEY and nothing else. FAKENET_-prefixed values
# describe the responder container's own view of the stack.

# --- Midnight endpoints (packages/lib/src/midnight-node-config.ts) ---
# Which Midnight network to run against (undeployed | stagenet | preview |
# preprod | mainnet); defaults to undeployed, the local docker stack.
# Networks other than undeployed target a deployed network over its public
# RPC. The proof server always stays local (it sees private witness data).
MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID=
# Endpoint overrides; default per MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID (undeployed = the local
# docker stack in docker-compose.yaml; *.midnight.network networks = their
# public endpoints). Stagenet's endpoints are NOT published in this repo, so
# on MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID=stagenet the node + indexer URLs below are REQUIRED
# (the WS twin derives from the indexer URL when unset).
MIDNIGHT_NODE_URL=
MIDNIGHT_INDEXER_URL=
MIDNIGHT_INDEXER_WS_URL=
MIDNIGHT_PROOF_SERVER_URL=

# --- Midnight wallet seeds (one funding root pays the others) ---
# Each is generated + persisted here on the first run; set one to reuse a
# wallet you already have (skips generation). All are 32-byte hex seeds, and
# a wallet's seed bytes double as its vault identity secret: the commitment
# computed from them (the vault's userCommitment circuit) is the identity
# that gates the vault's circuits.
#
# The funding wallet: holds NIGHT and pays it out to the other wallets the
# run needs (the deployer, the users, the MPC responder). It does no test
# work itself. On the local chain it defaults to the pre-funded genesis mint
# wallet. On a deployed network the first run generates it, stops, and
# prints its NIGHT address for faucet funding; a rerun then funds the others
# and proceeds.
MIDNIGHT_ROOT_WALLET_SEED=
# The contract deployer's wallet: pays the fees for deploying the signet and
# vault contracts. Its seed bytes are the deployer identity the deploy seals
# into the vault, so this same wallet is the only caller that passes the
# vault's deployer-gated initialize circuit.
MIDNIGHT_DEPLOYER_WALLET_SEED=
# User 1's Midnight wallet: the wallet the example's flows spend from. Its
# bytes are user 1's vault identity secret, whose commitment also serves as
# the MPC derivation path of user 1's EVM deposit address.
MIDNIGHT_USER1_WALLET_SEED=
# The fakenet MPC responder's wallet: pays the fees on the response
# transactions the responder submits. docker-compose interpolates it into
# the responder container.
MIDNIGHT_MPC_RESPONDER_WALLET_SEED=
# User 2's Midnight wallet: a second user for flows that need two parties.
# Today the bearer-transfer suite: user 2 receives the bearer token from
# user 1 and runs the withdraw, paying their own fees.
MIDNIGHT_USER2_WALLET_SEED=
# Faucet URL shown in underfunded-wallet hints (not published in this repo).
MIDNIGHT_FAUCET_URL=
# NIGHT amount (base units) to move from the root wallet into each wallet
# that needs funding. Unset splits the root's balance evenly across the
# wallets that need it.
FUND_WALLET_NIGHT_AMOUNT=
# Signing key of the maintenance authority the base deploy retains (32-byte
# hex). The contract is too large to register every circuit in one block, so
# the base deploy registers one and adds the rest as maintenance updates, each
# signed by this key. Keep it: it is the only way to add or replace a circuit
# afterwards. Unset generates an ephemeral key, which is fine only for a
# throwaway deploy: the contract is unmaintainable once the process exits.
MIDNIGHT_MAINTENANCE_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- EVM wallet seeds ---
# User 1's EVM wallet: independent of the Midnight seed, as two real wallets
# would be (one per chain). The account it derives at BIP-44 m/44'/60'/0'/0/0
# is EVM_USER1_WALLET_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS, dealt ETH + USDC on the local Sepolia fork.
# Generated + persisted here on the first run.
EVM_USER1_WALLET_SEED=

# --- Deployed contracts (appended by the integration suite) ---
# The signet contract on Midnight: the request/response bus between client
# contracts and the MPC network.
MIDNIGHT_SIGNET_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=
# The erc20-vault contract on Midnight: holds the deposit ledger and
# authorises withdrawals. Set it to reuse a deployment and skip the zk
# compile + deploy on reruns.
MIDNIGHT_VAULT_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=
# The ERC20 token contract the example's flows move. Defaults to real
# Sepolia USDC (present on the fork); the setup prints the value.
EVM_ERC20_CONTRACT_ADDRESS=

# --- MPC / fakenet keys (github.com/sig-net/solana-signet-program) ---
# The fakenet signer's root PRIVATE key. Every public key below derives from
# it, and the responder container receives it via compose interpolation.
# Generated per machine by the setup when unset. A real MPC network never
# exposes this: it exists here only because fakenet is a single-party
# stand-in.
MPC_ROOT_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The MPC root public key (compressed secp256k1): the public half of the
# root key. Deposit addresses epsilon-derive from this key + a contract
# address + a path.
MPC_ROOT_PUBLIC_KEY=
# The MPC's response-signing PUBLIC key for THIS vault contract: derived
# from the root public key + the vault contract address, so it exists only
# after the vault deploy. The initialize flow pins it on-chain, and the
# contract verifies MPC responses against it.
MPC_VAULT_RESPONSE_PUBLIC_KEY=

# --- Derived EVM accounts (appended by the integration suite) ---
# All three are derived and checked by the setup, never chosen, and dealt
# ETH + real USDC automatically on the local Sepolia fork.
#
# The vault's own EVM account: MPC-derived from MPC_ROOT_PUBLIC_KEY + the
# vault contract address at path "vault". Only the MPC network can sign for
# it. It custodies deposited tokens and needs gas ETH for withdrawals.
EVM_VAULT_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=
# User 1's DEPOSIT address: MPC-derived from MPC_ROOT_PUBLIC_KEY + the vault
# contract address, with user 1's identity commitment as the path. Only the
# MPC network can sign for it. The user funds it with tokens and gas, and a
# deposit is the MPC moving that balance into the vault's account.
EVM_USER1_DEPOSIT_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=
# User 1's own EVM WALLET account: the BIP-44 derivation of
# EVM_USER1_WALLET_SEED. The user controls this one, unlike the two
# MPC-derived accounts above.
EVM_USER1_WALLET_ACCOUNT_ADDRESS=

# --- EVM endpoints ---
# The e2e suites fork Sepolia on the local anvil so the real Uniswap V3
# deployment and real USDC are present. REQUIRED before `docker compose up -d`:
# compose adds `--fork-url` only when this is set (otherwise anvil is a bare
# chain with no USDC/Uniswap and the suites fail dealing tokens).
SEPOLIA_FORK_RPC_URL=
# Optional: pin a fork block for determinism. Needs an ARCHIVE RPC (state at an
# old block); leave unset to fork at latest.
#SEPOLIA_FORK_BLOCK=
# JSON-RPC endpoint of the EVM chain; defaults to the local `evm` docker
# compose service (http://127.0.0.1:8545, part of `docker compose up -d`).
EVM_RPC_URL=
# Resolved from the RPC when unset; verified against it when set (loud
# failure on mismatch — the value is sealed into the vault at initialize).
EVM_CHAIN_ID=

# --- Fakenet responder container (docker compose interpolates these) ---
# The container's own view of the stack: service-name hosts inside the
# compose network, never the host's 127.0.0.1 view. Defaults target the
# local compose stack. On a deployed network (e.g. stagenet) point the
# Midnight ones at that network's public endpoints so the responder polls
# the same chain the tests use (the proof server stays the local compose
# service). Both EVM sides must point at the SAME chain. The network id has
# no container-side twin: it is vantage-independent, so the container
# inherits MIDNIGHT_NETWORK_ID above directly.
#FAKENET_EVM_RPC_URL=http://evm:8545
#FAKENET_MIDNIGHT_INDEXER_URL=
#FAKENET_MIDNIGHT_INDEXER_WS_URL=
#FAKENET_MIDNIGHT_NODE_URL=
#FAKENET_MIDNIGHT_PROOF_SERVER_URL=
# Set to 0 to run the responder yourself (responder development) — the
# setup then leaves the container and .env alone.
#FAKENET_MANAGED=0
# The responder's HTTP endpoint as seen from the host; defaults to
# http://localhost:3040. The suites poll it for response status.
#FAKENET_RESPONSES_URL=

# --- Run-mode toggles (developer knobs a normal run leaves unset) ---
# The gate that lets the integration suites touch the network: unset, their
# setup pipeline is a no-op and every e2e test skips, so a plain `yarn test`
# stays offline. The `test:e2e` scripts set it, so set it yourself only when
# you invoke vitest directly.
#RUN_INTEGRATION_TESTS=1
# Pause and wait on the terminal before each setup step and before each flow
# test, so you can inspect the chain between steps.
#STEP_THROUGH=1
# Keep the local proof server running for the whole suite. Unset, the suite
# recycles it between test files so accumulated proving memory cannot kill it
# late in a long run. Set this when you run your own proof server.
#SKIP_PROOF_SERVER_RESTART=1
# CI only: skip the ~10-minute zk compile when the contract's managed keys
# directory already holds .prover files. Only an environment that restored
# those keys from a cache keyed on the contract sources may assert they are
# fresh, so a local run leaves this unset and lets the compile run.
#TRUST_PREBUILT_ZK_KEYS=1
# Where the compact launcher is installed, defaulting to ~/.compact. The static
# benchmark resolves the pinned toolchain's zkir-v3 binary through it.
#COMPACT_DIRECTORY=
# Fakenet responder container knobs, read by the compose service directly.
# The responder runs Midnight-only, so leave DISABLE_SOLANA at its default.
#VERBOSE=true
#DISABLE_SOLANA=true

# --- Resume (printed by a partial integration run) ---
# Request ids that let a rerun pick up an in-flight flow instead of creating a
# fresh request. Each flow prints its own on first creation, and the name is
# the flow's own: the ids below are the full set the suites read.
#DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#WITHDRAW_REQUEST_ID=
#FAILURE_REFUND_DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#FAILURE_REFUND_WITHDRAW_REQUEST_ID=
#DEPOSIT_CLAIMANT_NOT_CALLER_DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#FALSE_CLAIMER_DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#BEARER_TRANSFER_DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#BEARER_TRANSFER_WITHDRAW_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_WITHDRAW_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_SWAP_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_SUPPLY_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_REDEEM_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_REFUND_DEPOSIT_REQUEST_ID=
#BENCHMARK_REFUND_WITHDRAW_REQUEST_ID=
